INSERT INTO feature VALUES('activity-ledger','runtime','The work ledger of tasks per core','work-pool','implemented','notable',NULL,'Each worker of the pool writes a 24-byte mark at the start and the end of each task into a ring of its own, with one push, no lock and no cache line that another worker writes; a full ring drops its oldest mark and counts the drop. The hub drains the rings once for each tick, merges them by the clock, then by the core, and numbers each event in that order, so it is the one writer of the sequence number; an event earlier than the latest clock numbered takes the next number, is marked late and is counted. Each core''s occupancy over the last two seconds is 120 cells, which read the clock of each event. The pool''s recording fork marks each job on the ring of its thread, a sink of the instrument that answers the rings makes the judgement''s parse fork through it, and `gandr check --activity` prints each thread''s busy time, its drops and its late count. While a watcher follows the activity, one thread of the hub folds the rings once for each tick and sends each tick that has events to every watcher, and each judgement and each admission of the hub is one task on the ring of its thread. With no watcher, no thread folds and no job marks a ring. `gandr view` shows the activity pane at its foot: one row per core with its world, its occupancy over the last 32 ticks, the kind of the task that it runs now, its busy time over the window and the lengths of its tasks at p50 and p99, and a totals row that sums the cores. The hub folds the pane and sends it on the render bus for each tick that changes it, including each tick while busy time stays in the window. A cell of the occupancy holds at most one tick and each time column takes the unit of the window, so a row that moves leaves the cells of the other rows in place.','core-fork surface-dispatcher surface-session surface-lsp surface-lsp-core surface-driver surface-render-remote surface-tui','crates/core-fork/src/activity/tests.rs crates/core-fork/benches/activity.rs crates/surface-dispatcher/src/pool/recording/tests.rs crates/surface-dispatcher/src/walk.rs crates/surface-session/tests/instrument.rs crates/surface-lsp-core/src/activity/tests.rs crates/surface-lsp-core/src/activity/pane/tests.rs crates/surface-lsp/src/hub.rs crates/surface-tui/src/follow.rs crates/surface-driver/tests/cli.rs','crate-tests','#6298 #6450 #6299');
